 "notes": "Pathfinding-run 90% CL exclusion at the stationary TM020 resonance, 26.531 GHz (m_a = h f = 1.0972e-4 eV). Best limit g_agamma = 2.02e-12 quoted in abstract/conclusion as 'eV^-1', but this is a units typo: Fig. 3 axis is GeV^-1, the vector figure (e-print excnarrow.pdf) places the spike tip at ~2.1e-12 GeV^-1, and the quoted '~50x KSVZ' at 110 ueV also gives ~2e-12 GeV^-1. The figure draws the limit as a zero-width vertical spike from 2.02e-12 up to the CAST line (~6.6e-11), so the curve shape was reconstructed analytically: g(df) = 2.02e-12 * sqrt(1+(2 df/Dnu)^2) with Dnu = f0/QL, QL ~ 13,000 (loaded Q stated in text), i.e. the Lorentzian resonance shape the paper says sets the limit's ~2.5 neV span; truncated at the CAST level matching the top of the drawn spike. Paper's only stated DM density is 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (Ref. 35), so no rescaling applied. Figs. 4 and 5 are projections (Stage I/II) and were not extracted.",
